<p>Great article, I love it :) Kind of like a multiverse-dwelling version of the Foundation, except one that focuses purely on preservation of items, not world defense. I wonder whether there are any living beings that use, enjoy, or interact with the items in the archive, or if they are just preserved as an end in itself.</p>
<p>In regards to the alien font, I would think that a hyperdimensional multiverse-traveling alien civilization would have a writing system that's, well, weirder. At the very least it would be most likely logographic, not alphabetic, because they don't communicate by speech and also based on how you translated their responses in the logs - as in, more like Chinese than English, the characters would be more complicated and numerous/diverse and you wouldn't see the same ones pop up multiple times in a few sentences like you see in the image, except maybe for a few common ones like «MULTITUDE-GROUP» / «loc. WITHIN» / «BE/EXIST» / «HAVE». In addition, perhaps have it written vertically or in an even 5x5 square to create ambiguity as to how it's supposed to be read? I could make something like this for you if you want</p>

